A turnstile log holds "10 20 stray 30" in one stream. This fragment totals it:
Scanner sc = new Scanner("10 20 stray 30");
int t = 0;
while (sc.hasNextInt()) { t += sc.nextInt(); }
System.out.println(t);
What integer is printed?

A greenhouse log stores three labels across lines in "fern
 moss
 pine
". This fragment counts them:
Scanner sc = new Scanner("fern
 moss
 pine
");
int n = 0;
while (sc.hasNextLine()) { sc.nextLine(); n++; }
System.out.println(n);
What integer is printed?

A scoreboard parses pipe-separated laps with this fragment:
Scanner sc = new Scanner("17|42|8");
sc.useDelimiter("[|]");
int t = sc.nextInt() + sc.nextInt() + sc.nextInt();
System.out.println(t);
What integer is printed?

A tally file starts with a count followed by that many entries: "2\n40\n60\n". This fragment reads it:
Scanner sc = new Scanner("2\n40\n60\n");
int n = sc.nextInt();
int sum = 0;
for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) { sum += sc.nextInt(); }
System.out.println(sum);
What integer is printed?

A harvest log mixes commas and semicolons in "5, 7; 9". This fragment totals it:
Scanner sc = new Scanner("5, 7; 9");
sc.useDelimiter("[,;]\\s*");
int t = 0;
while (sc.hasNextInt()) { t += sc.nextInt(); }
System.out.println(t);
What integer is printed?

A rain reader tolerates one corrupt row with this fragment:
Scanner sc = new Scanner("12\nbad\n8\n");
int t = 0;
while (sc.hasNextLine()) {
  String line = sc.nextLine().trim();
  try { t += Integer.parseInt(line); }
  catch (NumberFormatException e) { }
}
System.out.println(t);
What integer is printed?

A ticket scanner must total an unknown count of integers and stop cleanly at a trailing word. Fill the blank:
Scanner sc = new Scanner("6 9 done 4");
int t = 0;
_____ { t += sc.nextInt(); }
System.out.println(t);
Which header prints 15?

A results row looks like "lena:82:91" and must split at every colon. Fill the blank:
Scanner row = new Scanner("lena:82:91");
row.useDelimiter(_____);
String name = row.next();
int total = row.nextInt() + row.nextInt();
Which argument yields total 173?

A log reader should echo every line of an unknown-length file but prints only the first:
if (sc.hasNextLine()) { System.out.println(sc.nextLine()); }
Which statement names the fault?

A counter crashes after its last value with this loop:
Scanner sc = new Scanner("3 8");
while (true) { System.out.println(sc.nextInt()); }
Which statement names the fault?

A cashier totals a stream with this fragment, but it never finishes on input "4 nope 6":
Scanner sc = new Scanner("4 nope 6");
int t = 0;
while (sc.hasNext()) {
  try { t += sc.nextInt(); }
  catch (InputMismatchException e) { }
}
Which statement names the fault?

A filter writes qualifying rows but the output file stays empty:
PrintWriter out = new PrintWriter("fast.txt");
for (String line : rows) { if (qualifies(line)) out.println(line); }
Which statement names the fault when no close or flush ever runs?

A trail program must report a friendly message when its data file is absent. Fill the blank:
try { sc = new Scanner(new File("trails.csv")); }
_____ { System.out.println("data file missing"); return; }
Which clause belongs in the blank?

A judge copies only passing scores into a new file. Fill the blank:
Scanner sc = new Scanner(new File("scores.csv"));
PrintWriter out = new PrintWriter("pass.txt");
sc.nextLine();
while (sc.hasNextLine()) {
  String line = sc.nextLine();
  int s = Integer.parseInt(line.split(",")[1].trim());
  _____ out.println(line);
}
Which line copies only scores of 60 or more?
